From 0be23139a5d091dd541f192622ac0043f77cd2bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:57:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): fuse indexer wq_b decode RoPE and MXFP4
 quantization

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Immediate base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a.

Fuse GPT-J interleaved RoPE on the trailing 64 columns of each 128-dim head and block-32 MXFP4 E2M1/UE8M0 quantization into the decode GEMM epilogue of indexer.wq_b (mxfp8_gemm_rope_mxfp4_decode).

Stage the 16x128 BF16 output tile into C_shared aliasing A_shared at buf_dyn_shmem + 0 after a cross-warp barrier (zero extra dynamic shared memory: 38,016 B total, 2 CTAs/SM = 96 CTAs/wave on GB10). Each 16-lane half-warp processes one 32-column scale group in registers (one adjacent column pair per lane, 64 registers/thread, 0 bytes stack frame) and reduces amax across the 16 lanes via four __shfl_xor_sync butterfly steps. Epilogue row iterations are guarded by warp-uniform m < M checks. DeepseekV4Attention._index_query routes unconditionally through project_block32_rope_mxfp4_decode at decode row counts (rows <= 64), eliminating 42 quantize_mxfp4 kernel launches per decode step and the [rows, 32, 128] BF16 intermediate buffer.

Quality: bit-identical (torch.equal on iq_data, iq_scale, and weights) to unfused wq_b followed by quantize_mxfp4 across all decode and verification batch sizes (rows in {1..48, 64}) in both eager and CUDA graph replay.

Tests: pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py (4 passed, 0 PDL violations) and 2-boot GPU container verification on GB10 (sp8).
Upstream status: local SM121 TileLang kernel optimization; not applicable upstream.
